"use strict";(globalThis.webpackChunkztools_docs=globalThis.webpackChunkztools_docs||[]).push([[48130],{77735(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"updates-and-allowances-2026-11","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/updates-and-allowances-2026-11","editUrl":"https://github.com/aoneahsan/ztools-docs/edit/main/blog/2026-11-10-updates-and-allowances.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-11-10-updates-and-allowances.md","title":"ZTools updates itself, and browser tools have no limit","description":"Open tabs now load a new ZTools release by themselves, browser tools need no account and have no usage limit, and one small promotion for another product from the same team.","date":"2026-11-10T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"ZTools releases and what changed in them."},{"inline":false,"label":"ZTools","permalink":"/blog/tags/ztools","description":"Posts about ZTools, its tools and how they work."}],"readingTime":1.12,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"The ZTools team","url":"https://ztools.zaions.com","page":null,"key":"ztools-team"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"updates-and-allowances-2026-11","title":"ZTools updates itself, and browser tools have no limit","description":"Open tabs now load a new ZTools release by themselves, browser tools need no account and have no usage limit, and one small promotion for another product from the same team.","authors":["ztools-team"],"tags":["release","ztools"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1794297685000,"nextItem":{"title":"What\'s new in ZTools: tours, a phone app view and plans","permalink":"/blog/whats-new-2026-10"}},"content":"You had ZTools open in a tab for a week. Until now, that tab could still be running last week\'s release. That changes today.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Updates reach open tabs\\n\\nA small worker now watches for a new release. It caches nothing. When one is out, the page loads it at a safe moment, and anything you\'ve typed stays where it was.\\n\\nSome releases are required. Then an update screen tells you why and offers one Update button. On Android, a new build comes through Google Play\'s in-app update, and smaller fixes arrive as signed over-the-air updates. [How ZTools stays up to date](/docs/guides/updates) has the details.\\n\\n## Browser tools: no limit, no account\\n\\nTools that run in your browser have no usage limit, and you don\'t need an account to use them.\\n\\nAllowances apply only where the work runs on our side: the AI assistant, Speak, and tools that process files on our server. Each feature shows its daily or monthly allowance beside it, and the amount depends on your plan. The [Plans page](https://ztools.zaions.com/growth/pricing) lists them.\\n\\n## One small promotion\\n\\nThe dashboard and tool pages now show one small ad, clearly marked. It\'s always for another product made by the ZTools team, never for ZTools itself. Plans that remove promotions don\'t show it.\\n\\nThe ZTools team"},{"id":"whats-new-2026-10","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/whats-new-2026-10","editUrl":"https://github.com/aoneahsan/ztools-docs/edit/main/blog/2026-10-27-whats-new.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-27-whats-new.md","title":"What\'s new in ZTools: tours, a phone app view and plans","description":"Page tours and a six-step walkthrough, an app view on phones, the Workbench design, and ZTools Pro and Growth Suite plans.","date":"2026-10-27T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"ZTools releases and what changed in them."},{"inline":false,"label":"ZTools","permalink":"/blog/tags/ztools","description":"Posts about ZTools, its tools and how they work."}],"readingTime":1.03,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"The ZTools team","url":"https://ztools.zaions.com","page":null,"key":"ztools-team"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"whats-new-2026-10","title":"What\'s new in ZTools: tours, a phone app view and plans","description":"Page tours and a six-step walkthrough, an app view on phones, the Workbench design, and ZTools Pro and Growth Suite plans.","authors":["ztools-team"],"tags":["release","ztools"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793088988000,"prevItem":{"title":"ZTools updates itself, and browser tools have no limit","permalink":"/blog/updates-and-allowances-2026-11"},"nextItem":{"title":"Welcome to the ZTools Blog","permalink":"/blog/welcome"}},"content":"Useful tools. One workbench. This release brings the Workbench design to the web app, an app view on phones,\\nguided tours, and plans you can buy.\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## Guided tours and a walkthrough\\n\\n- On the home page, Speak, Meeting notes, Plans, the dashboard and account settings, the tour button shows a short tour\\n  of that page. The first time you visit one of these pages, a hint says: \\"Take a quick tour of this page\\".\\n- [How ZTools works](https://ztools.zaions.com/walkthrough): six short screens show what ZTools does. Start anywhere.\\n\\n## An app view on phones\\n\\nOn a phone, home, the dashboard, account settings, sign-in and the first-run screens open as app screens, with a bottom\\nbar for Home, Dashboard, Speak, Plans and Account. Web and Android \xb7 Many tools work without signing in.\\n\\n## Plans\\n\\nZTools offers a free plan and paid plans. Each paid plan\'s price, billing period and allowances are shown on the\\n[Plans page](https://ztools.zaions.com/growth/pricing) before you pay. Payments are processed by Polar. ZTools never\\nreceives your card number.\\n\\n## Shared AI\\n\\nIf Anthropic\'s shared credit is unavailable, ZTools sends the same request from its server to OpenAI instead, within the\\nsame allowance. If neither can answer, AI pauses.\\n\\nThe ZTools team"},{"id":"welcome","metadata":{"permalink":"/blog/welcome","editUrl":"https://github.com/aoneahsan/ztools-docs/edit/main/blog/2026-05-06-welcome.md","source":"@site/blog/2026-05-06-welcome.md","title":"Welcome to the ZTools Blog","description":"This is the first post on the ZTools documentation blog. We\'ll use this space for:","date":"2026-05-06T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Release","permalink":"/blog/tags/release","description":"ZTools releases and what changed in them."},{"inline":false,"label":"ZTools","permalink":"/blog/tags/ztools","description":"Posts about ZTools, its tools and how they work."}],"readingTime":0.9,"hasTruncateMarker":true,"authors":[{"name":"Ahsan Mahmood","title":"Solo developer, ZTools \xb7 aoneahsan@gmail.com \xb7 +923046619706","url":"https://aoneahsan.com","page":null,"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/aoneahsan","linkedin":"https://www.linkedin.com/in/aoneahsan/","x":"https://x.com/aoneahsan"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/aoneahsan.png","key":"ahsan"}],"frontMatter":{"slug":"welcome","title":"Welcome to the ZTools Blog","authors":["ahsan"],"tags":["release","ztools"]},"unlisted":false,"lastUpdatedAt":1793429679000,"prevItem":{"title":"What\'s new in ZTools: tours, a phone app view and plans","permalink":"/blog/whats-new-2026-10"}},"content":"This is the first post on the ZTools documentation blog. We\'ll use this space for:\\n\\n- **Release notes** \u2014 what\'s new in each ZTools update\\n- **Tool spotlights** \u2014 deep-dives on individual tools and the problems they solve\\n- **Dev journal** \u2014 design decisions, technical tradeoffs, occasional mistakes\\n\\n\x3c!-- truncate --\x3e\\n\\n## What\'s shipped (May 2026)\\n\\n- **Tools live** at [ztools.zaions.com](https://ztools.zaions.com) \u2014 all browser-only, no signup, no upload\\n- **First wave of docs** \u2014 top 20 highest-demand tools documented with use cases, examples, and FAQs ([browse them \u2192](/docs/tools))\\n- **GitHub repo** for this docs site is open-source: [github.com/aoneahsan/ztools-docs](https://github.com/aoneahsan/ztools-docs)\\n- **Android app** shipped on Play Store; iOS pending Apple developer account approval\\n\\n## What\'s next\\n\\n- 15-20 tools per batch through batch 35+ until every documented tool from the app appears here\\n- Long-form how-to guides covering common workflows (compress images, format JSON, generate strong passwords)\\n- Algolia DocSearch integration for site-wide search\\n\\nIf there\'s a tool you\'d like documented sooner, [open an issue on GitHub](https://github.com/aoneahsan/ztools-docs/issues) and we\'ll bump it up the queue.\\n\\n\u2014 Ahsan"}]}}')}}]);